   "body": "**For Bybifok (operator decision, 2026-10-29): your findings are yours while the core is out of tokens.** Label `external: ready` added. Follow `docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Scope (check first, fix only if needed)**\n1. Write a test on LOT-041's endpoint builder (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRNetwork`) and on LOT-095's router (`HFRLinkRoute+Routing.swift`) proving that page N of a topic list is requested as `liste_sujet-N.htm` (or `forum1.php?…&page=N`), and never as `liste_sujet-1.htm?page=N`.\n2. If the test passes on `dev-swift`, the PR is tests only. Say so and close with `Closes #103`.\n3. If it fails, fix the builder or the router, nothing wider.\n4. The logged-in form of that URL is still a **pending capture** (HFR-PROTOCOL §7b B2, #278, Mac). Do not guess it: write \"pending capture\" and test only what the committed captures show.\n\n**Adversarial review (state it in the PR)**\n- Reviewer model ≠ author model (Opus author → Fable; Sonnet author → Opus).\n- The reviewer gets only: the diff, the PR's metadata lines, `docs/lots/LOT-041-*.md` and `docs/lots/LOT-095-*.md`, AGENTS.md, LESSONS.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and HFR-PROTOCOL.md.\n- It must check that every URL shape is traced to a capture or to legacy `file:line`, that the new test fails on the old code (mutation), and that no request leaves for the live forum.\n- Verdict format: EXTERNAL-AGENTS §7.\n\nCredit: Bybifok's finding (label kept).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
